Context: 2026-10-01 07:14 AEST the daemon (then up 2.5 days) was OOM-killed mid-webhook-flood (516 webhooks in final 4 min + concurrent briefing LLM turn; system load ~16, 30G zram in use). No supervisor existed (B829). User mandate: watch memory, analyze usage, implement optimizations (pre-authorized: code changes + daemon restarts), loop until 2 consecutive clean weeks.

Baseline 2026-10-02 00:53 (fresh daemon, 2h22m uptime): RSS 61MB / PSS 55MB / private-dirty 53MB (OCaml heap), swap 11.5MB, 7 threads, 14 fds. Daemon env has NO OCAMLRUNPARAM (default GC: space_overhead=120 -> heap may float ~2.2x live data). memory.db now 540MB (was 406MB in Sept - grew 33%).

Watch infrastructure:
- ~/.cache/clawq-memwatch/watch.sh (60s sampler -> mem.csv; events: RSS_CROSS 512M/1G/2G/4G/8G ladder, GROWTH >100MB/4min, DEAD) run under a persistent Monitor (re-armed on 10h caps).
- Daily scheduled review task (durable, 1d): trend analysis, daemon health, OOM journal check, bl append one-liner to this ticket, schedule re-creation near 7d expiry.
- Success criterion: no OOM/kill/leak-class growth for 14 consecutive days (clock started 2026-10-02, target 2026-10-16; resets on any incident).

Optimization candidates to evaluate (audit pending):
- GC tuning for the daemon process (space_overhead 80, possibly minor heap + capping policy) set via Gc in daemon init so all start paths inherit.
- Webhook flood guardrail: cap concurrent/in-flight webhook processing (B829 noted this).
- memory.db growth (540MB): retention/pruning of old rows; sqlite page cache per connection audit (many modules open connections).
- Session-state retention in long-lived daemon (200+ message histories observed in observer logs).
- Acceptance: each optimization lands with tests (x-p35 remote suite), fmt clean, review loop, daemon restart, and measurably moves RSS/flood-spike numbers; B830 notes get a dated one-liner daily.

Audit complete (2026-10-02). Root-cause chain for 61MB-fresh → OOM-2.5-days: (1) mgr.sessions Hashtbl never evicts — every github PR/issue key loads full history into heap forever (dominant steady-state leak); (2) OCaml 5.1 default GC (space_overhead=120, no compaction, no chunk decommit) turns every webhook-burst peak into permanent RSS; (3) webhook ingest is unbounded Lwt.async per delivery + unbounded body buffering + triple JSON parse + ignored rate limiter; (4) append-only tables (journal/deliveries/request_stats/outbox/correlations/ledger) never pruned, no vacuum → 540MB disk; (5) EC child 'seen' assoc list unbounded (true leak under error storms). Implementation decisions: Gc.set space_overhead=60 at daemon+EC start via shared helper + systemd unit Environment OCAMLRUNPARAM=o=60 + MemoryHigh=1G/MemoryMax=1.5G; idle-session eviction at 30min in 60s tick (guard active_scopes/pending_questions/queued_messages, lazy reload already exists); webhook worker pool of 4 + 1MB body cap + single-parse threading + honor rate limiter for fetch_pr_files + snapshots only post-filter; hourly retention sweep (journal 7d, deliveries 7d, request_stats 30d, egress_audit 7d purge wiring, correlations closed 7d, outbox terminal 7d, ledger 30d) + nightly VACUUM when db>200MB; EC seen pruned by cooldown age + cap 1000. Five lanes: b830a-eviction b830b-gc b830c-webhook b830d-retention b830e-ec-seen. Tests on x-p35 (no local test_main.exe runs).

DEPLOYED 2026-10-02 02:34 AEST: all five lanes merged to master (30b2b9cc; final gate fmt clean + 7,717 tests x-p35). Daemon restarted pid 619744 build 30b2b9cc: GC tuning live in daemon+EC (space_overhead=60 source=code), session eviction active (memory.session_idle_eviction_s=1800), webhook pool+body-cap+single-parse live, hourly retention sweep active (first sweep 1h post-boot; first vacuum in 02:00-05:00 window when db>200MB — expect the 540MB db to shrink overnight), EC seen bounded. Synthetic burst: 200x100KB unsigned pings in 0.2s -> all fast-rejected 403, RSS 23.9->33.2MB (+9MB held), real webhooks flowing normally seconds later, zero errors/drops. Fresh RSS 24-33MB (was 61MB at same age pre-fix). Follow-up filed: B831 raw/sanitized github key duality. 2-week clean clock running: started 2026-10-02, target 2026-10-16.

